      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transportation Kopa Safe</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Transporting a two-wheeler to Kopa Mau requires strict adherence to legal documentation standards to ensure a seamless transit experience. Engaging professional bike transport services in Kopa Mau simplifies this process, but the shipper remains responsible for providing accurate, verifiable paperwork.</p>
<p>These documents serve as the legal backbone of your shipment, protecting both your asset and the logistics provider. Meticulous preparation of these files prevents delays at transit hubs and ensures compliance with national road transport regulations.</p>

<p>The foundational requirement is a <strong>self-attested photocopy</strong> of the original Registration Certificate (RC). This document must clearly display the vehicle’s chassis number, engine number, and registration details. It is crucial that the name on the RC matches the consignor’s identity proof; any discrepancy can lead to immediate rejection of the shipment at the loading dock.</p>
<p>Additionally, you must submit a <strong>current Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate</strong>. Authorities mandate a valid PUC to verify that the vehicle meets environmental standards before it is permitted on public transport corridors. An expired certificate will halt the entire logistics chain, so ensure this document is within its validity period.</p>

<p>Financial protection is equally critical. You must provide a <strong>valid insurance certificate</strong> for the vehicle. More importantly, you should opt for <strong>100% declared-value marine transit insurance</strong>.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">This specific coverage type guarantees that the insurer will compensate the full market value of your bike in the event of accidental damage, theft, or total loss during transit.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Unlike basic third-party or comprehensive policies, marine transit insurance is tailored for goods in motion, offering comprehensive protection from the point of pickup to the final destination in Kopa Mau.</span></li></ul>

<p>Finally, the logistics provider will generate an <strong>IBA-approved consignment bilty</strong>. This is the official transport document that details the vehicle’s condition, dimensions, and agreed-upon freight charges. It serves as the contract between you and the transporter.</p>
<p>Ensure that the description on the bilty accurately reflects the bike’s make, model, and any visible pre-existing damages. Signing this document acknowledges the terms of service and the insurance coverage applied to your shipment.</p>
